{
  "id": "wbx-gfdd-si-01",
  "title": "Bank Z-score",
  "category": "markets",
  "icon": "💹",
  "desc": "It captures the probability of default of a country's banking system. Z-score compares the buffer of a country's banking system (capitalization and returns) with the volatility of those returns. It is estimated as (ROA+(equity/assets))/sd(ROA); sd(ROA) is the standard deviation of ROA. ROA, equity, and assets are country-level aggregate figures Calculated from underlying bank-by-bank unconsolidated data from Bankscope.",
